# Canonical verification classifications.
#
# Single source of truth for the FINAL_CLASSIFICATION field emitted by the
# installer and by tests/verify.sh. Both read this file rather than each
# hardcoding a label, because two copies of a label is how two reports come to
# disagree -- which happened once already, with CANARY_SUITE being emitted by one
# report and not the other.
#
# The label is release-scoped: it must name the release whose verification state
# it describes, so a report cannot silently carry a previous release's
# classification. tests/lib/static_checks.py asserts that the version digits in
# CLASSIFICATION_VERIFIED match the VERSION file, and fails if they drift.
#
# CLASSIFICATION_VERIFIED   all gates in this repository passed
# CLASSIFICATION_INCOMPLETE at least one gate did not
#
# A publication run (repository pushed, tag and release cut, and a clean target
# bootstrapped from the published URL) carries a separate, higher classification
# describing the publication, not the repository. That is recorded in the
# publication report, not here: this file describes the repository's own state.

CLASSIFICATION_VERIFIED=V1_0_1_HARDENING_VERIFIED
CLASSIFICATION_INCOMPLETE=V1_0_1_HARDENING_INCOMPLETE
